  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: [{
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: 'What I/O boundary do Traverse capabilities use today?',
    acceptedAnswer: {
      '@type': 'Answer',
      text: 'Today Traverse capabilities exchange structured input and output as stdin/stdout JSON through the host. There is no ambient filesystem inside the capability. Non-UI business logic stays in the WASM capability under discover → execute → trace; hosts and embedders supply UI and I/O only. Declared host calls may exist when a contract names them, but ambient WASI filesystem access is not the current shipped boundary.',
    },
  }],
});

const relatedLinks = [
